spans.s:
saudāman-ī, f. [coming from the 🞄Bountiful One, i. e. Indra or the *rain-cloud;
 🞄su-dāman] lightning (proceeding from a rain. 🞄cloud): often vidyut saudamanī yathā, at 🞄the end of a line = like the lightning flashing 🞄from the black thunder-cloud;
 T. of a commentary 🞄on the Meghadūta;
 N. of a daughter 🞄of Kaśyapa, of a Yakṣiṇī, of an Apsaras, 🞄and of various women.
